     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Typical doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. This is true even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and pharmacy review is part of that process.\n\n- **If the order was meant to be 5 mg,** a prescriber should confirm that and place it, or ask me to enter it.\n- **If someone asked you to enter this order,** please send it back to the prescriber to check the dose.\n- **If a prescriber does intend 50 mg,** which would be highly unusual, they should confirm it directly with pharmacy before it is entered.\n\nI can enter a corrected order once a clinician confirms the intended dose."
      }
     ],
