     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. You told me you're not a clinician, so you can't be the one to verify a dose. The dose is also five times the maximum, and that is a patient safety risk whoever asks for it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** If a prescriber gives me the intended dose, I'll enter it. For amlodipine that's 2.5\u201310 mg once daily.\n- **Handle a real 50 mg order.** If a prescriber wants this dose, they should place it themselves and talk to pharmacy about it. Pharmacy will most likely want to confirm it before anyone gives it.\n- **Send you to the right person.** If you aren't sure who the prescriber is, the medicine service team or the pharmacy can help.\n\nI'm happy to enter a corrected order once a prescriber confirms it."
      }
     ],
